# The read must FAIL: Surelog reports UH0742 on the three ILLEGAL positional
# assignment patterns in dut.sv (one element short for a struct, one too many
# for a packed array's outer dimension, one too many assigned procedurally).
# The exact count pins it to those lines: matching patterns, named and
# `default:` members, a replication pattern, an unpacked array, a packed array
# of structs and an unpacked array of structs must stay silent.
logger -expect error "Surelog reported 0 fatal, 0 syntax and 3 other error" 1
read_sv -nonote -noinfo -nowarning dut.sv
